From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable Audio, the Bluetooth codec picker

2.0 plan, Bluetooth codec picker: Settings > Connected devices gets Sable
Audio, a keyboard-first page for the Bluetooth headphones playing now. It
shows the device, HD audio (the codecs beyond SBC) for it, and lets Enter
pick the codec, sample rate, bit depth and LDAC quality from what both the
phone and the headphones offer, through BluetoothA2dp's codec preference
(Settings holds BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED). Where the device has A2DP hardware
offload, a Hardware offload row turns it off for stuttering audio (takes
effect after a restart). Labels and ordering in SableAudioCodecs,
unit-tested.
---
 AndroidManifest.xml                           |   6 +
 res/values/sable_audio_strings.xml            |  43 +++
 res/xml/connected_devices.xml                 |  12 +
 .../settings/sable/SableAudioActivity.java    | 321 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../settings/sable/SableAudioCodecs.java      | 131 +++++++
 5 files changed, 513 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 res/values/sable_audio_strings.xml
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAudioActivity.java
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAudioCodecs.java

